read ai/codex/hint.md before starting work.

Goals:
1. First inspect relevant code and determine whether removing the thin client layer is actually a better design.
2. Create a new git branch under the ai/codex prefix before making changes.
3. If the thin client layer is removed, push ttl.afterJitter() down into the appropriate xxxSupport layer.
4. Change Spring registration / bean wiring / constructor injection only if necessary.
5. Do not change business logic or cache semantics.
6. Write a change document, or a “why no change” document, into ai/codex/refactor.

Required workflow:
1. Inspect the codebase first. Do not refactor blindly.
   - Review all classes under common-util/src/main/java/com/exchange/common/redis/cache/client
