   - Preserve existing cache behavior, version behavior, tombstone behavior, negative-cache behavior, delete behavior, logging behavior, and parse-error recovery behavior
   - Update constructor dependencies, interfaces, and bean registrations only as needed
   - Do not change business-facing logic or behavior
   - Prefer the smallest safe refactor that improves structure

5. Validation:
   - Update imports and registrations cleanly
   - you can skip test, but make sure there is no compile-time error

6. Documentation:
